  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nPersistent high pressure remains over New Mexico and the Texas\nPanhandle Tuesday through the end of the week. The pattern changes\nslightly over the weekend as the high regresses west slightly\ncausing more northerly flow over the Great Plains allowing for a\nweak cold front to drop south. Models are indicating this front\ncould make it as far south as our CWA allowing for some hope for\nrainfall. These rain chances are not currently reflected in the\nNBM forecast, but I suspect later runs will start increasing PoPs\nfor the weekend if the trend holds. Otherwise triple digit heat\nand dry conditions to continue.\n\nHennig",
